)\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/buffer-lua#buffer.copy_stream:dst-dstoffset-src-srcoffset-count)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:buffer.copy_stream","jsName":"copyStream","line":127,"member":"copy_stream","modulePath":["buffer"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the destination stream","optional":false,"rawName":"dst","rawType":"buffer_stream"},{"description":"the offset to start copying data to (measured in value type)","optional":false,"rawName":"dstoffset","rawType":"number"},{"description":"the source data stream","optional":false,"rawName":"src","rawType":"buffer_stream"},{"description":"the offset to start copying data from (measured in value type)","optional":false,"rawName":"srcoffset","rawType":"number"},{"description":"the number of values to copy (measured in value type)","optional":false,"rawName":"count","rawType":"number"}],"rawName":"buffer.copy_stream","returnDescriptions":[],"returns":[],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/buffer.lua"},{"description":"Create a new data buffer containing a specified set of streams. A data buffer\ncan contain one or more streams with typed data. This is useful for managing\ncompound data, for instance a vertex buffer could contain separate streams for\nvertex position, color, normal etc.\n\n**Examples:**\n\nHow to create and initialize a buffer\n\n```lua\nfunction init(self)\n  local size = 128\n  self.image = buffer.create( size * size, { {name=hash(\"rgb\"), type=buffer.VALUE_TYPE_UINT8, count=3 } })\n  self.imagestream = buffer.get_stream(self.image, hash(\"rgb\"))\n\n  for y=0,self.height-1 do\n     for x=0,self.width-1 do\n         local index = y * self.width * 3 + x * 3 + 1\n         self.imagestream[index + 0] = self.r\n         self.imagestream[index + 1] = self.g\n         self.imagestream[index + 2] = self.b\n     end\n  end\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/buffer-lua#buffer.create:element_count-declarat